Open Vanilla 0040: Boss Fights, raids at level 60 by queue, a fresh copy of the raid for every group, in the
hangout Duels already has.

OpenVanilla.BossFights = 1 (off by default) on the Duels world server. One hangout, two modes: the lobby is
Duels' hangout (OpenVanilla.Duels.Hub, .Hub.Fence: Gurubashi Arena, where every new character starts); owner,
2026-10-23: "instantly start them in the gurubashi arena that shares with duelers, but separate game mode".
A character is a dueler or a raider (bossfights_player.mode): Duels' hangout code skips raiders (fence,
outfits, consumables, its bots), Boss Fights acts only on raiders, and each keeps its own queue, windows and
results. ".wnl wf bf go" (at once, from anywhere on the realm) or a raid queue makes a dueler a raider and
takes it off the Duels queue; Duels' "join" makes it a dueler again (not mid-run). "mode boss|duels" (the
addon, from the site's link) switches without a port and marks the account for 30 minutes, so a new
character made then starts as a raider; the character screen stays. The queue (".wnl wf bf q <raid> [tier]",
default 10 players, 2 tanks and 2 healers until the oldest ticket has waited 120 s, parties never split; a
leader's playerbots count as members) makes one raid group and binds every member to a new instance of the
raid made for that group alone (as Warfront's arena), entry checks skipped. Creatures in a run's copy are
scaled by tier, the run's size and the tier's affixes (fortified, tyrannical, enrage): health in
Creature::AddToWorld, damage in Unit::*DamageBonusTaken. Encounters come from the copy's completed mask; the
run is timed from the first pull, with splits, deaths and wipes. A clear opens the next tier
(bossfights_progress), raises the tier aura (+2% stats per tier, at most 10%) and Warfront's armory tier.
World buffs and consumables on entering. Results (runs with bots marked, ranked apart), boards and the runs
now for the website (bossfights_result, bossfights_now, warfront_live row 2). SQL and the stack:
realm/bossfights, hetzner/bossfights_up.sh.

