+/*
+ * Open Vanilla — Boss Fights (GPLv2, as CMaNGOS). See BossFights.h for the player's path, the settings and the
+ * protocol; BossFightsLogic.h for the pure rules (tested in realm/bossfights/tests).
+ *
+ * Threads: commands and the per-player part run on the player's map thread (Update); queues, groups, instance
+ * binds and the runs' clocks on the world thread before the maps update (WorldUpdate). Both sides meet under
+ * g_lock. The damage and spawn hooks run on any map thread and only read the per-instance scale table.
+ *
+ * A raid "slice" per group: at the pop the world thread makes a new instance id and its persistent state
+ * (sMapPersistentStateMgr.AddPersistentState), binds every member to it permanently (a permanent player
+ * save wins over any group save in MapManager::CreateInstance, so nobody's own lockout is used and nobody
+ * else can follow them in) and makes them one raid group; the port uses TELE_TO_SKIP_ENTRY_CHECKS and the
+ * entrance checks are skipped for run members (MovementHandler, Map). When the run ends and a member is out,
+ * the bind goes (UnbindInstance) and the empty copy unloads (Instance.UnloadDelay). Warfront's arena makes
+ * its Ring of Law copies the same way.
+ */
+
